  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Pisonin A may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Pisonin A to A172, which is a target of Feigrisolide C, and Feigrisolide C is known to target Phosphodiesterase 6C. The second pathway connects Pisonin A to A172, which is also a target of another compound, 3-O-beta-D-glucopyranosyl-oleanolic acid 28 O-beta-D-glucopyranoside, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The third pathway shows that Pisonin A targets DNA polymerase eta, which is a target of a complex molecule that ultimately targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings collectively indicate that Pisonin A may exert its effects on Phosphodiesterase 6C through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving various targets and signaling pathways. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the relationships are inferred through multiple indirect links, and the exact nature of the interactions remains uncertain without further experimental validation.",
